@startuml state-transitions
title US-13: Alert State Machine (including SUPERSEDED for composite alerts)

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam stateBorderColor #555555
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam stateArrowColor #333333

[*] --> NEW : alert evaluator publishes\nalert event to Kafka\nAPI writes initial record

NEW --> ACKNOWLEDGED : operator clicks Acknowledge\nPATCH /alerts/:alert_id\n{ status: ACKNOWLEDGED }

ACKNOWLEDGED --> RESOLVED : operator clicks Resolve\nPATCH /alerts/:alert_id\n{ status: RESOLVED }

NEW --> RESOLVED : operator skips acknowledge\nand resolves directly

NEW --> SUPERSEDED : system-only\natomic transaction on composite detection\n(UPDATE status=SUPERSEDED, superseded_by=$composite_id)

SUPERSEDED --> [*]

RESOLVED --> [*]

note right of NEW
  alert_id deterministic:
    SIGNAL_LOSS: {entity_id}:SIGNAL_LOSS:{dark_since_ms}
    UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY: {pair_key}:UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY:{episode_start_ms}
    ROUTE_DEVIATION: {entity_id}:ROUTE_DEVIATION:{episode_start_ms}
    COMPOSITE: {pair_key}:COMPOSITE:{dark_since_ms}
  Duplicate insert is a no-op via ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING.
end note

note right of ACKNOWLEDGED
  Records who acknowledged and when.
  Other operators see the alert is owned.
  Alert evaluator continues evaluating —
  it does not read lifecycle state.
end note

note right of SUPERSEDED
  System-only transition — cannot be set by operator PATCH.
  Occurs atomically with COMPOSITE alert insertion.
  superseded_by column (nullable FK) references the COMPOSITE alert.
  Dashboard shows SUPERSEDED alerts in evidence/history view.
  Not deletable — part of the audit trail.
end note

note right of RESOLVED
  Record is never deleted — it is the audit trail.
  If the anomaly recurs, a new alert_id is generated
  (new window_start_ms or episode_start_ms) —
  a fresh record, not a reopen.
end note

@enduml
